04:11.670 --> 04:13.920
whether I cloned it or forked and cloned.

04:13.920 --> 04:17.220
You have permission to make commits on your own local repo.

04:17.220 --> 04:18.630
But what I don't have permission to do

04:18.630 --> 04:20.640
unless I own the repository

04:20.640 --> 04:23.340
or I've been granted collaborator privileges,

04:23.340 --> 04:25.246
is push as we already know.

04:25.246 --> 04:29.130
So I own this repository because I forked it.

04:29.130 --> 04:30.300
So I can push up

04:30.300 --> 04:33.292
and push that new change to my fork,

04:33.292 --> 04:35.790
git remote dash V.

04:35.790 --> 04:37.983
So if I push my master branch to origin,

04:39.030 --> 04:41.070
just like that, git push origin master.

04:41.070 --> 04:44.610
Now my new commit is on my fork

04:44.610 --> 04:46.770
and we see change color palette, right?

04:46.770 --> 04:49.080
All the other commits are like years and years ago,

04:49.080 --> 04:50.925
